 "section_summary": "This section contains educational records for Kochi Prefecture, Japan, compiled in 1946 during the Allied occupation. It comprises statistical tables detailing educational institutions, student enrollments, and teaching personnel by administrative jurisdiction and school level, followed by Part Three of the survey consisting of a title page and the first 48 pages of a comprehensive school roster. The roster documents Ministry of Education, prefectural, municipal, and town and village schools—including youth schools and 275 elementary schools—recording locations, founding dates, gender-disaggregated enrollments, and faculty counts as of April and November 1946.",
